From: GE-Proton <git@localhost>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 05:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winepulse: Retarget Sony effects on profile changes

PipeWire replaces a Sony controller's sink when switching between Default
and Direct profiles. Applications may keep their effect streams alive across
that replacement, and ALSA may continue reporting the old PipeWire PCM as
connected. The endpoint-churn guard consequently rejects the new target,
leaving both actuator and controller-speaker channels on the removed profile
until the controller is physically replugged.

Treat a different ALSA PipeWire target as an intentional profile migration.
Close the old PCM and reconnect existing Windows streams to the newly
published profile. Keep the connected-PCM guard for repeated discovery of
the same target, where no migration is needed.
---
 dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c b/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
--- a/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
+++ b/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
@@ -3205,11 +3205,14 @@ static HRESULT pulse_retarget_dualsense_haptic_stream_path(struct pulse_stream
     snd_pcm_state_t state;
     char *path;
     HRESULT hr;
+    BOOL target_changed;
 
     if (!stream->dualsense_haptic_registered)
         return S_FALSE;
+    target_changed = !stream->haptic_alsa_path || strcmp(stream->haptic_alsa_path, target);
     if (stream->haptic_pcm &&
-            (state = snd_pcm_state(stream->haptic_pcm)) != SND_PCM_STATE_DISCONNECTED)
+            (state = snd_pcm_state(stream->haptic_pcm)) != SND_PCM_STATE_DISCONNECTED &&
+            !target_changed)
     {
         TRACE("Keeping connected Sony controller haptic stream %p on %s during endpoint churn "
                 "(PCM state %s).\n", stream, debugstr_a(stream->haptic_alsa_path),
-- 
